          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fe44f88c4985ce72dd8133b32e255062c3bfcd01",
          "message": "Merge feature/operator-fusion-jb: operator fusion + the design review\n\nMixed Select/Where/prune chains now collapse to one wrapper\n(SelectWhereTreenumerable) behind an internal two-interface recipe\nsurface: ISelectWhereTreenumerable (Relabels + Compose(resultSelector,\nrelabels)) and ISelectTreenumerable (the projection fast path,\nreviving the original interface). CompositionResult... became\nSelectWhereResult, a bare (value, strategies) pair. Arity-split\nvalue/positional overloads are the fusion surface; the join rule\ngates positional lambdas on Relabels; the struct-generic\nIResultSelector seam keeps plain operators at zero cost (measured\nfaster than pre-fusion main on the degenerate rows).\n\nValidated by the combinatorial battery (fused vs forced-stacked,\n8-operator alphabet x 584 chains x consumer interference, both\ndimensions) plus targeted pins; all 24,322 tests green. New Compose\nbenchmark family measures the collapse win: DFT 1.3-1.6x, BFT 9-13x.\n\nDesign record: docs/OPERATOR_FUSION_DESIGN.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
