          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b3c87e14b755cf3994f875b9f1b370b97ea98dce",
          "message": "Fusion doc: the positional overload is (TNode, NodePosition), not NodeContext\n\nCompiler-verified: a bare Func<TNode,bool> overload beside the\nNodeContext overload is CS0121-ambiguous for any lambda whose body binds\nunder both (x => true, parameter-ignoring closures, node types with a\nNode/Depth member); the arity split resolves always -- LINQ's (x, i)\nshape exists for the same reason. NodeContext exits the public\noperator-lambda surface (stays treenumerator-level); the migration is a\nfull-surface alpha break sized as its own workstream. Bonus refinement:\npositional Selects still self-fuse (Select's emission boundary is the\nidentity on positions); only positional Where refuses its own kind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
