          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f0374169dff4076213dde2897dc69405e1a51794",
          "message": "PruneAfter over PruneAfter merges by predicate union, keeping the bespoke driver\n\nThe first CI run after the fusion merge caught it (PruneAfter\nTriangle rows ~2x allocation): the canonical Mega trees are built\nwith PruneAfter, so PruneAfter.Triangle_HalfDepth is\nPruneAfter-over-PruneAfter -- which composed through ToSelectWhere\nonto the Where driver, paying promotion path state a never-rejecting\nchain cannot use. Previously filed as a niche periphery item; the\nsuite's own tree idiom promoted it.\n\nThe fix is the filed design: the PruneAfter operator probes the\nconcrete wrapper first (type-preserving, no erasure issue) and\nmerges predicates -- prune when either matches, inner-first\nshort-circuit preserving lambda order -- into one bespoke wrapper.\nBoth flavors qualify (the wrapper never relabels). Trees, labels,\nand order are equivalent to stacked; evaluation counts differ only\nwhere the purity contract permits.\n\nMeasured: Triangle rows return to the pre-fusion baseline\n(59.3 -> 29.9 KB DFT, 227.0 -> 113.8 KB BFT). The combinatorial\nbattery's aa/aA/Aa/AA chains gate the merge; all 24,322 tests green.\n\nThe Select.Composition +0.3 KB is the arity-split's per-operator\nadapter closure at construction time -- constant per pipeline,\naccepted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
